  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Department of Justice: 39 references to former U.S. Code sections or former act names (48 CFR)",
      "summary": "In the CFR chapters assigned to the Department of Justice in 48 CFR, 39 references in 39 sections use a former address or name: 39 cite a section replaced by a new one when the title was enacted as positive law. Each reference was compared with release point 119-134 of the U.S. Code, which names where the old number went.",
      "impact": "A reader who follows these references finds a note that the section moved, or no section, instead of the text. A reference to a moved section may keep its legal effect, but the address no longer leads to the text. No effect on a decision or an amount has been established.",
      "correction": "The agency decides how to update each reference. Where the U.S. Code names the section the old number moved to, the evidence below gives it."
    }
  },
